<p>Use this menu to make settings about paper sources.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="inputtray" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span></p>
<p>Select an input tray.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you cannot select the desired input tray, check 
 that all installed options are configured on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab of the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Auto Tray 
 Select</span>, the printer uses paper from another input tray that contains 
 paper of the same size and type if there is no more paper left in the 
 current tray.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="bypasstray" role="heading">Position in bypass tray...</p>
<p>Select the orientation of the paper placed on the bypass tray.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="type" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type:</span></p>
<p>Specify the type of printing medium you want to use. Available media 
 types differ depending on the printer you are using.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Plain &amp; Recycled (Auto. for Postcard)</span>, it is normally printed as plain paper/recycled paper. If the print paper size is postcard, print with a paper type suitable for postcards.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="tabstock" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">[Tab Stock] Printing</span></p>
<p>Select this in order to print a portrait document with the tab on the 
 right and a landscape document with the tab on the top.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="shift" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Shift Print Position for [Tab Stock]</span></p>
<p>Prints the image by shifting the image toward the tab so that you can 
 print on the tab and also have extra space on the opposite side for stapling 
 or punching.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="letter" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Letterhead Setting:</span></p>
<p>Specify whether or not to print using the letterhead setting.<br/>
This function enables you to print correctly on paper that has a fixed 
 print side or print direction such as letterhead paper, for example.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>For details about loading in the paper tray paper 
 that has a fixed print side or print direction, see the operating instructions 
 provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Printer Default</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Follows the printer settings.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Off</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Disables the letterhead printing.<br/>
When two-sided printing with an odd paged job is enabled, letterhead paper 
 might not be printed correctly.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Auto Detect</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Performs the letterhead printing when paper that 
 has a fixed print side or print direction is specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Paper 
 Type:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">On (Always)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Always performs the letterhead printing.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="apply" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Apply [Letterhead Setting] to 1 sided 
 print</span></p>
<p>Specify whether or not to apply the letterhead setting to one-sided 
 printing.<br/>
Apply this to one-sided printing to print on letterhead paper correctly.</p>
